# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true and deployed to Linux. Without this
# file, every shell script is checked out with CRLF line endings, and a CRLF shebang fails on the
# VM with `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` - which reads as a missing
# interpreter rather than as a line-ending problem.
#
# startup.sh is the worst case: it is uploaded as VM metadata, so it breaks on a machine you
# cannot see, during a boot you are not watching.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
